    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling offensive output today, anchored by the elite 80.98 score of **Pete Crow-Armstrong**. Facing a favorable matchup against Kodai Senga, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from a massive 18% skill boost against the opposing starter and a +10% cushion from the leadoff spot; his combination of elite speed and favorable park factors makes him our premier start. **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** also anchor the lineup against Zack Littell, with both boasting strong 70+ efficiency ratings. **Trea Turner** remains our primary catalyst for stolen bases, and despite a slight negative adjustment for the high probability of a stolen base attempt against Littell, his top-of-the-order usage keeps his floor exceptionally high.\n\nWe are hunting upside in the middle-infield and OF spots today, specifically with **Caleb Durbin**, whose 70.67 score is fueled by a significant 19% boost from facing the struggling Sean Sullivan. **Caleb Durbin**'s profile is critical in our strategy to corner the scarce SB category. **Dillon Dingler** and **Casey Schmitt** round out our aggressive platoon plays; **Casey Schmitt** in particular sees his value elevated by favorable wind conditions and an 11% platoon advantage. **Yordan Alvarez** serves as our stabilizer, maintaining a strong 64.32 score despite facing a tougher opponent in Shane Bieber, as his elite xwOBA of 0.448 provides a buffer against the matchup risk.\n\nThe decision to bench **Carson Benge** was the most difficult, as his 56.71 score narrowly missed the cut behind **Kazuma Okamoto**. While **Carson Benge** benefits from the leadoff slot, the optimizer favored **Kazuma Okamoto** due to the aggregate projection against Peter Lambert. We are monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters closely; specifically, **Christian Yelich** carries a high risk today due to a 13% negative platoon adjustment against Nick Lodolo, leaving him as our lowest-rated starter. We will be ready to pivot to **Colt Keith** or **Lars Nootbaar** if the final lineups reveal that our primary hitters are dropped in the batting order, which would immediate erode the \"Order\" bonus currently buoying their scores.",
